        explanation:'Backpropagation computes gradients through the computational graph. SGD updates parameters using a mini-batch gradient; momentum accumulates a velocity that dampens oscillation. Adam maintains moving averages of first and second moments and adapts per-parameter step sizes. Learning-rate warmup can stabilize early transformer training; cosine or step decay reduces the rate later. Gradient clipping limits exploding updates but does not fix incorrect labels or a broken loss. Monitor training and validation loss, gradient norms, activation statistics and throughput. Use a fixed seed for debugging but evaluate across seeds when variance matters.',
        keyPoints:['Learning rate is often the most influential optimization hyperparameter.','Momentum and Adam smooth or adapt updates but do not guarantee generalization.','Warmup and decay shape optimization over the training schedule.','Gradient clipping controls extreme updates; it does not repair data bugs.','Track gradient norms and validation metrics alongside loss.'],
