        analogy:'A team that practices only one exact script may fail when conditions change. Regularization introduces controlled variation and prevents the model from depending on brittle shortcuts.',
        explanation:'Weight decay discourages large weights; in AdamW it is decoupled from the adaptive gradient update. Dropout randomly masks activations during training and is disabled at evaluation. Batch normalization uses batch statistics during training and running estimates at inference; LayerNorm normalizes within each example and is common in transformers. Early stopping selects a checkpoint based on validation behavior. Data augmentation changes inputs while preserving labels when the transformation is semantically valid. These methods have interactions: applying every regularizer at maximum strength can cause underfitting.',
