        id:'rag-chunking-context-design',title:'RAG chunking, metadata filters and context assembly',level:'Advanced',duration:'85 min',
        why:'Retrieval quality is often limited by how documents are segmented and filtered, not by the language model’s ability to write a fluent answer.',
        analogy:'A library can own every book but still fail a reader if pages are torn into random strips and the catalogue has no useful labels.',
        explanation:'Chunk size controls how much local context is embedded and retrieved. Small chunks improve specificity but can lose surrounding meaning; large chunks preserve context but dilute semantic similarity and consume prompt budget. Use structural boundaries such as headings, paragraphs and tables before applying token-based limits. Overlap can preserve continuity but creates duplication. Attach source, tenant, document version, section and timestamps as metadata. Apply authorization filters before candidate retrieval and again before returning evidence. Rerank a bounded candidate set, deduplicate adjacent chunks and assemble context under a token budget. Preserve citations to exact source spans.',
        keyPoints:['Chunk by document structure before using fixed token windows.','Overlap reduces boundary loss but increases duplicate retrieval.','Metadata filters should enforce authorization, not just improve relevance.','Rerank only a bounded candidate set.','Context assembly needs deduplication, source spans and token budgeting.'],
        workedExample:'A policy document has headings, numbered clauses and tables. Split by clause, retain heading paths and page spans, then subdivide unusually long clauses. Search returns the relevant clause and neighboring context rather than arbitrary 500-character fragments.',
        code:'def assemble_context(hits, token_budget, tokenizer):\n    chosen, seen, used = [], set(), 0\n    for hit in hits:  # already authorized and reranked\n        key = (hit.document_id, hit.start, hit.end)\n        if key in seen:\n            continue\n        cost = len(tokenizer.encode(hit.text))\n        if used + cost > token_budget:\n            continue\n        chosen.append({"text": hit.text, "source": hit.source, "span": [hit.start, hit.end]})\n        seen.add(key); used += cost\n    return chosen',
