          question:{prompt:'What is the purpose of a durable checkpoint?',options:['To store every prompt forever','To resume from a verified state without repeating completed side effects','To bypass authorization after restart','To make all operations exactly-once automatically'],explanation:'Checkpoints preserve verified progress; idempotency and reconciliation are still needed to control duplicate side effects.'},
          project:'Design a durable refund-request state machine with retry classification, idempotency, human approval and recovery after a simulated process restart.',
          pitfalls:['Assuming a database transaction spans external APIs.','Retrying every error identically.','Resuming with stale permissions.','Calling a workflow completed before the final postcondition is verified.'],next:'Memory design, state summaries and context management'
